{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire HD 8 interests me because a portable entertainment screen would add a different use alongside my Echo and Fire TV devices.",
    "The Blink bundle connects my earlier interest in door alarms with my recent Alexa devices, adding video monitoring I would consider useful. Ring also fits that interest, but I would explore Blink instead of buying both."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Echo Dot and additional Fire TV sticks repeat functions covered by my fourth-generation Dot, Echo Show and recent Fire TV Stick 4K Max bundle.",
    "The earbuds do not address a current listening need, and my Mac-compatible keyboards do not establish that I own an iPhone or want AirPods.",
    "The SSD enclosure relates to my storage purchases, but I have no identified spare M.2 drive that would make it useful now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Echo and Fire TV purchases seem to be taken as interest in more devices from those lines, even when the suggested devices add little to what I already have.",
    "My computer accessory purchases seem to be treated as interest in loosely related accessories without a specific task or compatibility need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they show which needs I have already covered; an older or overlapping device needs a clear additional purpose.",
    "I am more interested in additions that extend what I can do, such as portable viewing or Alexa-compatible video security, than in repeating an existing setup.",
    "A specialized accessory needs a matching device or concrete use, and interest in two security options does not mean I would buy overlapping systems."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in connected home electronics but often confuse a useful addition with another device that repeats a need I have already covered."
}"}
